<title>JAPAN: TIFFE Euroyen ease by close, BOJ accommodative.</title>
<headline>TIFFE Euroyen ease by close, BOJ accommodative.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>April 14 settlement April 11 settlement</p>
<p> TIFFE Euroyen 3M (Z)	99.04		   99.05</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The key December Euroyen deposit rate futures on TIFFE ended marginally easier, mainly due to dealers' position adjustment amid a market belief that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) will not change its easy credit stance any time soon, traders said.</p>
<p>The BOJ drained only 600 billion yen from the market, which had a projected surplus of 710 billion yen before the central bank's operation at 0020 GMT.</p>
